## Findings

1. blocking — brief:58 — The agent-written zero-floor and formatting rules turn an exhausted estimate into “About 1 hour left.” The captures show this on W-2 after nine hours and W-6 after one day, against the eight-hour completed-sample median; the display falsely keeps completion an hour away — replace with: “When estimated remaining time reaches zero, show ‘Taking longer than usual (estimate)’ alongside recorded elapsed time.” — check: prototype apps/web/src/screens/BoardView.tsx:41; W-413-b2 overdue assertions; board-1280-collapsed.png.
2. blocking — brief:21 — The agent-written timing branch treats every non-Done card as active work. A Halted card retaining `start`, including fixture W-8, receives a completion countdown despite its “Stopped” stage explanation — replace with: “Halted cards may retain factual elapsed-time text, for example ‘Started 3 days ago’, but show ‘Stopped; no completion estimate’ and never a remaining-time forecast.” — check: prototype apps/web/src/lib/board.ts:399; W-413-b2 retained-start Halted case and a Halted-column capture.

